{{!
  The desktop entry the .deb and the .rpm install as
  /usr/share/applications/nazar-tray.desktop.

  It is the bundler's own default with two keys added, and both of them are about the one
  way this application is unusual: launching it opens nothing.

    StartupNotify=false           There is no window to wait for. Without this a launcher
                                  shows a busy cursor until it gives up, and a user who
                                  clicked the menu entry is told the program did not
                                  respond -- while it is running, in the tray, correctly.

    X-GNOME-UsesNotifications=true  This is a notifier: threshold toasts are the reason it
                                  is in the tray rather than in a terminal. The key is what
                                  puts nazar-tray in GNOME's own Notifications settings, so
                                  the user can silence it where they silence everything
                                  else -- next to the quiet hours in the panel, not instead
                                  of them.

  Everything else is a template variable, so bundle.category, the short description and the
  binary name stay in tauri.conf.json and cannot drift from what the Windows installer says.
  No localised Name or Comment: the six languages live in ui/locales/*.json and this file
  has no way to read them, and a translation kept in a second place is a translation that
  goes stale.
}}
[Desktop Entry]
Categories={{categories}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}}
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Name={{name}}
Terminal=false
Type=Application
StartupNotify=false
X-GNOME-UsesNotifications=true
{{#if mime_type}}
MimeType={{mime_type}}
{{/if}}
